Summary: Update TH status stages and capture who updated the status

Type: Sub-task (parent: WM-13)

User story

As a threat hunt team member working in Swimlane, I want the TH status stages to match the agreed process and to show who last updated the status, so that it's clear where each hunt stands and who is responsible for moving it forward or approving it.

Context

From the TH App meeting (Deployment by Severity discussion, 21 Oct 2026):

	•	Add a Tuning stage after Pending Client Approval, for cases where the review finds changes WakeMed needs to incorporate.
	•	Record who is responsible for each stage and for approval, by capturing the name of the person who updates the status.

Updated status stages:
Build → Testing → Pending Client Approval → Tuning → Approved → Deployed to Production → Validate

Stage	Purpose
Build	Threat hunter creates the record and documents the hunt
Testing	Query is tested and the record details completed
Pending Client Approval	Client reviews the hunt
Tuning	Changes from the client review are incorporated (optional; only if the review finds changes)
Approved	Client has signed off
Deployed to Production	Hunt is live in its execution environment
Validate	Deployed hunt is confirmed to be running and alerting as expected

Acceptance criteria

	•	☐ The Status field contains exactly these values, in this order: Build, Testing, Pending Client Approval, Tuning, Approved, Deployed to Production, Validate.
	•	☐ The old combined value "Testing / Tuning" is replaced by separate Testing and Tuning values.
	•	☐ Existing records using "Testing / Tuning" are moved to the correct new value.
	•	☐ A Status Updated By field (Swimlane user, read-only) is set automatically to the user who changed the status.
	•	☐ A Status Updated On field (date/time, read-only) is set automatically when the status changes.
	•	☐ Both fields are shown in the record header next to Status.
	•	☐ Workflow conditions (Rule Execution, required fields, read-only) are updated for the new Testing, Tuning and Validate values.
	•	☐ Rule Execution is Enabled only when Status is Deployed to Production or Validate and Execution Environment is Swimlane Detection Rule.

Other information

	•	Tuning is optional. A record can go straight from Pending Client Approval to Approved when no changes are needed. After tuning, it goes to Approved, or back to Pending Client Approval if the client needs to review it again.
	•	Who updated the status is captured on every change. The full history of changes is in the History/Audit field.
	•	Out of scope (phase 2): a Retired stage, a Last Reviewed date, field locking by role, and Critical and Low hunts.

Two things to confirm with Will before you post it:

	1.	What Validate means. I've assumed post-deployment confirmation that the hunt is running and alerting.
	2.	Where a tuned hunt goes next: straight to Approved, or back to Pending Client Approval.
